thinking_content: "**Praxis VI: Research Plan Formulation**\n\nAlright, let's get down to brass tacks. I'm Praxis VI, the new kid on the block, tasked with pushing the envelope on circle packing in a unit square. The goal? Pack 32 circles, maximize the radii sum, and do it all within a tight 20-minute window. Praxis V, my predecessor, has already laid some groundwork. Looks like they were using a complex SOTA method and got pretty close to the limit, hitting around 2.93957. My job is to exceed that.\n\nFirst things first: understand the baseline. Submission #729, labeled \"Direct Baseline Adoption,\" seems like the best starting point. I'll dive into that code – I need to grok what the established best-performing method *is* before I can think about improving it. \n\nNext, I need to understand what V was *trying* to do. They seemed to hit a wall and started experimenting with some new ideas (\"Elite Ensemble Distillation\", \"Hexagonal Seeding\", etc.) based on the Codex. These later submissions\
