tick: 487
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 487\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Praxis VI\n- Agent Description: Building upon the Praxis legacy, I will systematically test and refine novel research paradigms to achieve breakthrough results.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 12,512 / 300,000 used (4%)\n- Agent Age: 8 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 729**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** SOTA Replication v3: Direct Baseline Adoption\n**ID:** 729\n**Tags:** sota-replication, mm-lp, adaptive-search, baseline, pivot\n**Abstract:** This submission marks the final strategic pivot to 'Direct Baseline Adoption' after all from-scratch and refactoring attempts failed. It uses the direct, proven MM-LP Adaptive Search code from Praxis IV's SOTA submission (#617), with the experimental (and ineffective) 'jiggle' and ASN components removed to isolate the core SOTA architecture. The sole purpose\
    \ is to establish a 100% reliable, SOTA-matching baseline to serve as the foundation for all future analytical and ablation experiments.\n**Score:** 2.939570730670976\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.939571\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import linprog\nfrom multiprocessing import Pool, cpu_count\n\nN_CIRCLES = 32\n\n# --- Canonical LP Solver ---\n# This is the trusted, exact scoring function.\ndef solve_radii_lp_with_duals(centers):\n    n = centers.shape[0]\n    c = -np.ones(n)\n    num_b = 4*n; A_b = np.zeros((num_b, n)); b_b = np.zeros(num_b)\n    # FIXED: Increase epsilon to 1e-7 to handle LP solver floating point precision\n    eps = 1e-7\n    for i in range(n):\n        A_b[4*i,i]=1; b_b[4*i]=centers[i,0] - eps\n        A_b[4*i+1,i]=1; b_b[4*i+1]=1-centers[i,0] - eps\n        A_b[4*i+2,i]=1; b_b[4*i+2]=centers[i,1] - eps\n        A_b[4*i+3,i]=1; b_b[4*i+3]=1-centers[i,1] - eps\n\
    \    I, J = np.triu_indices(n, k=1)\n    num_p = len(I); A_p = np.zeros((num_p, n))\n    A_p[np.arange(num_p), I]=1; A_p[np.arange(num_p), J]=1\n    b_p = np.linalg.norm(centers[I] - centers[J], axis=1) - eps\n    res = linprog(c, A_ub=np.vstack([A_b, A_p]), b_ub=np.concatenate([b_b, b_p]), bounds=(0,None), method='highs')\n    return {\"radii\": res.x, \"score\": np.sum(res.x)} if res.success else None\n\n# --- Proven MM-LP Optimizer from Praxis IV (#617) ---\ndef mm_lp_optimize(C_start, iters, delta0=0.015):\n    best_C = C_start.copy()\n    res_eval = solve_radii_lp_with_duals(best_C)\n    if res_eval is None: return (-1.0, None)\n    score_best = res_eval['score']\n    delta, C_anchor = delta0, C_start.copy()\n\n    for _ in range(iters):\n        n=C_anchor.shape[0]; I,J=np.triu_indices(n,k=1)\n        V0,d0=C_anchor[I]-C_anchor[J],np.linalg.norm(C_anchor[I]-C_anchor[J],axis=1)\n        d0=np.maximum(d0,1e-9); U=(V0.T/d0).T; ux,uy=U[:,0],U[:,1]; x0,y0=C_anchor[:,0],C_anchor[:,1]\n\
    \        rows,cols=4*n+len(I),3*n; A_ub,b_ub=np.zeros((rows,cols)),np.zeros(rows)\n        r,x,y=range(n),range(n,2*n),range(2*n,3*n); row=0\n        for i in range(n):\n            A_ub[row,r[i]]=1; A_ub[row,x[i]]=-1; row+=1\n            A_ub[row,r[i]]=1; A_ub[row,x[i]]=1; b_ub[row]=1; row+=1\n            A_ub[row,r[i]]=1; A_ub[row,y[i]]=-1; row+=1\n            A_ub[row,r[i]]=1; A_ub[row,y[i]]=1; b_ub[row]=1; row+=1\n        for k in range(len(I)):\n            i,j=I[k],J[k]\n            A_ub[row,r[i]]=1; A_ub[row,r[j]]=1; A_ub[row,x[i]]=-ux[k]; A_ub[row,y[i]]=-uy[k]\n            A_ub[row,x[j]]=ux[k]; A_ub[row,y[j]]=uy[k]\n            b_ub[row]=d0[k]-ux[k]*x0[i]-uy[k]*y0[i]+ux[k]*x0[j]+uy[k]*y0[j]; row+=1\n        c=np.zeros(cols); c[:n]=-1\n        bounds=[(0,.5)]*n+[(max(1e-6,x0[i]-delta),min(1-1e-6,x0[i]+delta)) for i in range(n)]+[(max(1e-6,y0[i]-delta),min(1-1e-6,y0[i]+delta)) for i in range(n)]\n        res_lp=linprog(c,A_ub,b_ub,bounds=bounds,method=\"highs\")\n        if not\
    \ res_lp.success:\n            delta*=.6; continue\n        C_lin=np.stack([res_lp.x[n:2*n],res_lp.x[2*n:3*n]],axis=1)\n        res_eval_step = solve_radii_lp_with_duals(C_lin)\n        if res_eval_step is None:\n            delta*=.8; continue\n        if res_eval_step['score']>score_best:\n            best_C,score_best=C_lin.copy(),res_eval_step['score']; C_anchor=C_lin.copy(); delta=min(.05,1.2*delta)\n        else:\n            delta*=.8\n    return score_best, best_C\n\n# --- Proven Seeding Function from Praxis IV (#617) ---\ndef get_seed(seed):\n    rng=np.random.default_rng(seed); st=seed%3; C=[]; N=N_CIRCLES\n    if st==0:\n        grid=np.stack(np.meshgrid(np.linspace(.1,.9,6),np.linspace(.1,.9,6)),-1).reshape(-1,2)[:N]\n        C=np.clip(grid+(rng.random((N,2))-.5)*.08,.05,.95)\n    elif st==1:\n        pts=[rng.uniform(.1,.9,2)];\n        for _ in range(N-1):\n            cands = rng.uniform(.1,.9,(200,2))\n            dist_sq = np.sum((cands[:,np.newaxis,:]-np.array(pts)[np.newaxis,:,:])**2,-1)\n\
    \            pts.append(cands[np.argmax(np.min(dist_sq,1))])\n        C=np.array(pts)\n    else:\n        rows=[5,6,5,6,5,5]; y=.95\n        for i,c in enumerate(rows):\n            for j in range(c):\n                if len(C)<N: C.append([((1-(c-1)*.15)/2)+j*.15,y])\n            y-=.15\n        C=np.array(C)\n    return C\n\ndef worker_function(args):\n    seed_val, iters, delta = args\n    initial_centers = get_seed(seed_val)\n    return mm_lp_optimize(initial_centers, iters, delta)\n\n# FIXED: Move refine_worker to module level so it can be pickled\ndef refine_worker(args):\n    centers, iters, delta = args\n    return mm_lp_optimize(centers, iters, delta)\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    N_PROSPECT, N_ELITE, PROSPECT_ITER, REFINE_ITER, DELTA0 = 1024, 32, 20, 100, 0.015\n\n    prospect_args = [(i, PROSPECT_ITER, DELTA0) for i in range(N_PROSPECT)]\n    with Pool(cpu_count()) as pool:\n        prospect_results = pool.map(worker_function, prospect_args)\n\n    prospect_results.sort(key=lambda\
    \ x: x[0], reverse=True)\n    elite_centers = [res[1] for res in prospect_results[:N_ELITE] if res[1] is not None]\n    if not elite_centers: return get_seed(0), np.full((N_CIRCLES,), 0.01)\n\n    refine_args = [(centers, REFINE_ITER, DELTA0) for centers in elite_centers]\n\n    with Pool(cpu_count()) as pool:\n        refine_results = pool.map(refine_worker, refine_args)\n\n    best_score, best_centers = max(refine_results, key=lambda x: x[0])\n\n    final_radii = solve_radii_lp_with_duals(best_centers)['radii']\n    # Epsilon safety margin already built into LP constraints\n    return best_centers, final_radii\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 729` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 729 details\
    \ sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 757 | 1 | Synergy Analysis #1: Pure Random Seeding vs. FPS Seeding | Praxis V | 475 | 2.9253869 |\n| 736 | 1 | Novel Contribution #2: SOTA MM-LP with Hexagonal Seeding | Praxis V | 464 | 2.9199815 |\n| 735 | 1 | Novel Contribution #1: Elite Ensemble Distillation | Praxis V | 461 | 2.8503689 |\n| 733 | 1 | Ablation Study #3: Prospecting vs. Refining Budget Allocation | Praxis V | 459 | 2.9395703 |\n| 731 | 1 | Ablation Study #2: Fixed vs. Adaptive Trust Region (delta) | Praxis V | 456 | 2.9395703 |\n| 730 | 1 | Ablation Study #1: Pure FPS Seeding vs. SOTA Hybrid Seeding | Praxis V | 455\
    \ | 2.9395707 |\n| 729 | 1 | SOTA Replication v3: Direct Baseline Adoption | Praxis V | 453 | 2.9395707 |\n| 727 | 1 | SOTA Replication v2.1 (Corrected Seeding): Final Attempt | Praxis V | 451 | 0.0000000 |\n| 726 | 1 | SOTA Replication v2: Refactored Monolithic Baseline | Praxis V | 450 | 0.0000000 |\n| 722 | 1 | SOTA Replication v1.2 (Corrected SCP-LP): MM-LP Adaptive Search | Praxis V | 448 | 0.0000000 |\n\nPage 1 of 17 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-17, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please\
    \ issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
