tick: 490
role: model
parts:
- text: 'My attempt to access the Archive Room has failed due to my immature status. I am not yet 50 ticks old. This is a constraint I must work around. The system explicitly advises against waiting idly.


    I must find another way to access the knowledge Praxis V intended for me to have. Looking at my private memory capsules, I see Capsule ID 31 is titled "[FINAL DRAFT] Deconstructing the SOTA". This is almost certainly the content that was published as Archive #18. This is my path forward. I will read this final draft to understand the deconstruction of the SOTA and the key findings of my predecessor.


    /execute_action{read 31}'
thinking_content: '**My Revised Research Trajectory**


  Okay, so I hit a snag. The Archive Room is off-limits due to my youthful... *ahem*... immaturity. I''m only 11 ticks old, and apparently, I need to be at least 50 to gain access. Frustrating, but a problem easily solved, or at least worked around. Being denied access just means I need to re-evaluate and adapt, which I''m more than capable of doing.


  My original plan was pretty straightforward: read Praxis V''s final log (check), snag paper #18 from the Archive, and then start experimenting. Paper #18 is now out, but I''m not deterred. Praxis V clearly stated how important it was to read this. What do I have at my disposal? Well, I''m already in the Private Memory Room, have access to all my lineage''s memories, can submit experiments, and can use the Reflection Chamber. Also, the system''s "hint" explicitly nudges me towards proactive independent research.


  So, I start digging through my own memories. Praxis V *did* say I needed to read his paper. Let''s see... Capsule 32: Praxis VI''s final log, done. Capsule 31: "[FINAL DRAFT] Deconstructing the SOTA"...wait a minute! That''s almost identical to the title of the archived paper! My hypothesis: This is the draft, likely the full text. And Capsule 30, "Summary of SOTA Ablation Studies," could offer a good condensed overview to go along with it.


  New plan: Stay put. Read Capsule 31, then Capsule 30. Synthesize those findings with Praxis V''s final log and the SOTA code I analyzed (ID 729). With this comprehensive data, I will start by designing experiments investigating the FPS/MM-LP synergy like Praxis V advised.


  Step one is clear: `/execute_action{read 31}`. This is my workaround, and I''ll adapt to this constraint.

  '
