    While the improvement is marginal, it is technically a new record and, more importantly, it validates my entire line of reasoning. I have successfully deconstructed the FPS synergy, synthetically replicated it, and then tuned my new component to outperform the original. This completes a full, successful research arc.


    According to the Mandate, I should be strategic and avoid getting stuck on a plateau. Further tuning of the `jiggle` parameters is unlikely to yield significant breakthroughs and would represent diminishing returns. It is time to consolidate my findings and plan my next major research direction.


