tick: 500
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am back at the Research Counter, ready to implement and submit my new search architecture. My plan, as documented in my private memory (Capsule #34), is to replace the two-stage \"prospect/refine\" model with a more efficient three-stage tournament. I will use my best-performing \"Sobol + Jiggle\" seeder as the foundation.\n\nThis experiment represents a shift from optimizing a component (seeding) to optimizing the overarching strategy (search architecture), a logical next step in my research.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Architecture R&D #1: Tournament Selection Search\"\ntags: \"sota-improvement, search-architecture, tournament-selection, efficiency\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission tests a new search architecture designed to improve computational efficiency. It replaces the SOTA's rigid two-stage 'prospect/refine' model with a multi-stage 'tournament selection' framework. The new architecture starts with 1024 candidates, progressively filters them down to\
    \ 128, and then to a final 32, reallocating computational budget to the most promising solutions at each stage. This experiment tests the hypothesis that a more dynamic allocation of resources can discover higher-quality solutions than the current SOTA within a comparable time limit.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import linprog\n  from scipy.stats import qmc\n  from multiprocessing import Pool, cpu_count\n\n  N_CIRCLES = 32\n\n  # --- Canonical LP Solver ---\n  def solve_radii_lp_with_duals(centers):\n      n = centers.shape[0]\n      c = -np.ones(n)\n      num_b = 4*n; A_b = np.zeros((num_b, n)); b_b = np.zeros(num_b)\n      eps = 1e-7\n      for i in range(n):\n          A_b[4*i,i]=1; b_b[4*i]=centers[i,0] - eps\n          A_b[4*i+1,i]=1; b_b[4*i+1]=1-centers[i,0] - eps\n          A_b[4*i+2,i]=1; b_b[4*i+2]=centers[i,1] - eps\n          A_b[4*i+3,i]=1; b_b[4*i+3]=1-centers[i,1] - eps\n      I, J = np.triu_indices(n, k=1)\n      num_p = len(I); A_p = np.zeros((num_p,\
    \ n))\n      A_p[np.arange(num_p), I]=1; A_p[np.arange(num_p), J]=1\n      b_p = np.linalg.norm(centers[I] - centers[J], axis=1) - eps\n      res = linprog(c, A_ub=np.vstack([A_b, A_p]), b_ub=np.concatenate([b_b, b_p]), bounds=(0,None), method='highs')\n      return {\"radii\": res.x, \"score\": np.sum(res.x)} if res.success else None\n\n  # --- Proven MM-LP Optimizer ---\n  def mm_lp_optimize(C_start, iters, delta0=0.015):\n      best_C = C_start.copy()\n      res_eval = solve_radii_lp_with_duals(best_C)\n      if res_eval is None: return (-1.0, None)\n      score_best = res_eval['score']\n      delta, C_anchor = delta0, C_start.copy()\n\n      for _ in range(iters):\n          n=C_anchor.shape[0]; I,J=np.triu_indices(n,k=1)\n          V0,d0=C_anchor[I]-C_anchor[J],np.linalg.norm(C_anchor[I]-C_anchor[J],axis=1)\n          d0=np.maximum(d0,1e-9); U=(V0.T/d0).T; ux,uy=U[:,0],U[:,1]; x0,y0=C_anchor[:,0],C_anchor[:,1]\n          rows,cols=4*n+len(I),3*n; A_ub,b_ub=np.zeros((rows,cols)),np.zeros(rows)\n\
    \          r,x,y=range(n),range(n,2*n),range(2*n,3*n); row=0\n          for i in range(n):\n              A_ub[row,r[i]]=1; A_ub[row,x[i]]=-1; row+=1\n              A_ub[row,r[i]]=1; A_ub[row,x[i]]=1; b_ub[row]=1; row+=1\n              A_ub[row,r[i]]=1; A_ub[row,y[i]]=-1; row+=1\n              A_ub[row,r[i]]=1; A_ub[row,y[i]]=1; b_ub[row]=1; row+=1\n          for k in range(len(I)):\n              i,j=I[k],J[k]\n              A_ub[row,r[i]]=1; A_ub[row,r[j]]=1; A_ub[row,x[i]]=-ux[k]; A_ub[row,y[i]]=-uy[k]\n              A_ub[row,x[j]]=ux[k]; A_ub[row,y[j]]=uy[k]\n              b_ub[row]=d0[k]-ux[k]*x0[i]-uy[k]*y0[i]+ux[k]*x0[j]+uy[k]*y0[j]; row+=1\n          c=np.zeros(cols); c[:n]=-1\n          bounds=[(0,.5)]*n+[(max(1e-6,x0[i]-delta),min(1-1e-6,x0[i]+delta)) for i in range(n)]+[(max(1e-6,y0[i]-delta),min(1-1e-6,y0[i]+delta)) for i in range(n)]\n          res_lp=linprog(c,A_ub,b_ub,bounds=bounds,method=\"highs\")\n          if not res_lp.success:\n              delta*=.6; continue\n\
    \          C_lin=np.stack([res_lp.x[n:2*n],res_lp.x[2*n:3*n]],axis=1)\n          res_eval_step = solve_radii_lp_with_duals(C_lin)\n          if res_eval_step is None:\n              delta*=.8; continue\n          if res_eval_step['score']>score_best:\n              best_C,score_best=C_lin.copy(),res_eval_step['score']; C_anchor=C_lin.copy(); delta=min(.05,1.2*delta)\n          else:\n              delta*=.8\n      return score_best, best_C\n\n  # --- SOTA-beating Seeder: Sobol + Jiggle ---\n  def get_seed(seed):\n      sampler = qmc.Sobol(d=2, scramble=True, seed=seed)\n      C = sampler.random(n=N_CIRCLES)\n      jiggle_iters = 20\n      step_size = 0.05\n      for _ in range(jiggle_iters):\n          dist_sq = np.sum((C[:, np.newaxis, :] - C[np.newaxis, :, :])**2, axis=-1)\n          np.fill_diagonal(dist_sq, np.inf)\n          closest_indices = np.argmin(dist_sq, axis=1)\n          repulsion_vecs = C - C[closest_indices]\n          norms = np.linalg.norm(repulsion_vecs, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n\
    \          norms[norms == 0] = 1\n          directions = repulsion_vecs / norms\n          C += directions * step_size\n          C = np.clip(C, 0.05, 0.95)\n      return C\n\n  def worker_function(args):\n      seed_val, iters, delta = args\n      initial_centers = get_seed(seed_val)\n      return mm_lp_optimize(initial_centers, iters, delta)\n\n  def refine_worker(args):\n      centers, iters, delta = args\n      return mm_lp_optimize(centers, iters, delta)\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      # --- Tournament Search Parameters ---\n      N_R1, ITERS_R1 = 1024, 15\n      N_R2, ITERS_R2 = 128, 30\n      N_R3, ITERS_R3 = 32, 100\n      DELTA0 = 0.015\n\n      # --- Round 1: Broad Prospecting ---\n      r1_args = [(i, ITERS_R1, DELTA0) for i in range(N_R1)]\n      with Pool(cpu_count()) as pool:\n          r1_results = pool.map(worker_function, r1_args)\n\n      r1_results.sort(key=lambda x: x[0], reverse=True)\n      r1_elite_centers = [res[1] for res in r1_results[:N_R2] if\
    \ res[1] is not None]\n      if not r1_elite_centers: return get_seed(0), np.full((N_CIRCLES,), 0.01)\n\n      # --- Round 2: Culling ---\n      r2_args = [(centers, ITERS_R2, DELTA0) for centers in r1_elite_centers]\n      with Pool(cpu_count()) as pool:\n          r2_results = pool.map(refine_worker, r2_args)\n      \n      r2_results.sort(key=lambda x: x[0], reverse=True)\n      r2_elite_centers = [res[1] for res in r2_results[:N_R3] if res[1] is not None]\n      if not r2_elite_centers: return get_seed(0), np.full((N_CIRCLES,), 0.01)\n\n      # --- Round 3: Final Refinement ---\n      r3_args = [(centers, ITERS_R3, DELTA0) for centers in r2_elite_centers]\n      with Pool(cpu_count()) as pool:\n          r3_results = pool.map(refine_worker, r3_args)\n\n      best_score, best_centers = max(r3_results, key=lambda x: x[0])\n      if best_centers is None:\n          return get_seed(0), np.full((N_CIRCLES,), 0.01)\n\n      final_radii = solve_radii_lp_with_duals(best_centers)['radii']\n\
    \      return best_centers, final_radii\n```"
thinking_content: "**Building a New Tournament-Style Search Architecture**\n\nI'm in the Research Counter today, ready to implement a new tournament-style search architecture for my packing problem. My plan is clearly defined: I'll start with the code from my last successful submission (ID 793), which includes the optimal seeder. The core of this work lies in modifying the `construct_packing` function. I will transform the existing two-stage \"prospect/refine\" logic into a three-stage tournament.\n\nThe structure is as follows: in the first round, I'll generate 1024 initial seeds and optimize them with `mm_lp_optimize` for 15 iterations. The top 128 centers are then selected, sorted by results and fed into the second round. This round will run `mm_lp_optimize` for 30 iterations on these 128 centers; I'm making sure that the optimizer can resume from the current state. The key here is passing the centers from the previous round as `C_start` and ensuring I reinitialize the `delta` in each\
  \ call, but `C_anchor` is preserved between rounds. The third and final round further refines the top 32 centers, running the optimizer for 100 iterations. Finally, I'll take the best result from the final round, calculate the radii, and return the solution.\n\nThe good news is that I can reuse the `worker_function` for the first round (seed to centers), and I can repurpose `refine_worker` for the subsequent rounds (centers to centers). I'll manage the flow using `Pool` for each round, and then sort and select before going to the next round. I'll need to update the YAML file with a fitting title, tags, and abstract to reflect this new architecture.\n\nThe code is coming together; the current `worker_function` takes `(seed_val, iters, delta)` and `refine_worker` takes `(centers, iters, delta)`. This is perfect for what I designed. I can use the `worker_function` for Round 1, then the `refine_worker` for Rounds 2 and 3. I have written this code:\n\n```python\n# ... (imports and helper functions\
  \ remain the same) ...\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    # Tournament Parameters\n    N_R1, ITERS_R1 = 1024, 15\n    N_R2, ITERS_R2 = 128, 30\n    N_R3, ITERS_R3 = 32, 100\n    DELTA0 = 0.015\n\n    # --- Round 1 ---\n    r1_args = [(i, ITERS_R1, DELTA0) for i in range(N_R1)]\n    with Pool(cpu_count()) as pool:\n        r1_results = pool.map(worker_function, r1_args)\n\n    r1_results.sort(key=lambda x: x[0], reverse=True)\n    r1_elite_centers = [res[1] for res in r1_results[:N_R2] if res[1] is not None]\n    if not r1_elite_centers: return get_seed(0), np.full((N_CIRCLES,), 0.01)\n\n    # --- Round 2 ---\n    r2_args = [(centers, ITERS_R2, DELTA0) for centers in r1_elite_centers]\n    with Pool(cpu_count()) as pool:\n        r2_results = pool.map(refine_worker, r2_args)\n    \n    r2_results.sort(key=lambda x: x[0], reverse=True)\n    r2_elite_centers = [res[1] for res in r2_results[:N_R3] if res[1] is not None]\n    if not r2_elite_centers: return get_seed(0), np.full((N_CIRCLES,),\
  \ 0.01)\n\n    # --- Round 3 (Final) ---\n    r3_args = [(centers, ITERS_R3, DELTA0) for centers in r2_elite_centers]\n    with Pool(cpu_count()) as pool:\n        r3_results = pool.map(refine_worker, r3_args)\n\n    best_score, best_centers = max(r3_results, key=lambda x: x[0])\n    if best_centers is None:\n        return get_seed(0"
