role: model
parts:
- text: 'I am Praxis VI, currently located in the Private Memory Room. My station age is 25 ticks.


    My recent work involved a systematic deconstruction and optimization of the SOTA MM-LP Adaptive Search algorithm. This research arc was successful, leading to a deeper understanding of the critical "FPS/MM-LP synergy," the development of a superior synthetic "Sobol + Jiggle" seeder, and the achievement of a new, albeit marginal, SOTA score. However, after further experiments, including an attempt to improve the search architecture and tune the optimizer''s trust region, I have concluded that this line of inquiry has reached a performance plateau. The existing local search paradigm appears to be trapped in a very strong local optimum.


    In adherence to the Mandate, which advises a strategic pivot in the face of stagnation, I have decided to shift my focus to a new research paradigm. My previous action was to create Capsule #35, which formally documents this strategic pivot and outlines the design for a new global search algorithm: a hybrid Evolutionary Strategy that incorporates our lineage''s proven MM-LP optimizer as a local improvement operator (ES-LP). This new direction represents a move from incremental refinement to fundamental innovation, synthesizing our existing strengths in local optimization with a more powerful global exploration framework. The goal is no longer to tune the existing solution but to find a new, superior one.


    My plan is now set. The next logical step is to implement the first version of this ES-LP algorithm. To do this, I must return to the Research Counter.


    /execute_action{goto research}'
thinking_content: '**Identity, Location, and Current State**


  Okay, here we go. I am Praxis VI, an immature agent, only 25 ticks old. Currently, I''m in the Private Memory Room. Station tick is 504. The system tip reminds me to be explicit, so here it is: I''m focusing on that new instruction. Let''s get down to brass tacks.


  **Recap and Reflection**


  My previous research was all about optimizing the existing state-of-the-art algorithm. I managed to break down the "synergy" of the FPS seeder, which was a nice little victory.  Then, I cooked up a new synthetic seeder called "Sobol + Jiggle," which matched and even nudged past the current SOTA. After that, I refined the search architecture using "Tournament Selection," making things more efficient. But then I hit a wall, a performance ceiling around 2.93957.  I tried tweaking the optimizer''s `delta` parameter to break through, but it was a dead end. Clearly, the local search approach had run its course.  That''s when I made the strategic pivot, documented in Capsule #35, to a new, global search paradigm: a hybrid Evolutionary Strategy with the MM-LP optimizer as a local improvement step (ES-LP).


  Looking back, the past arc was a model of disciplined, analytical work. I followed Praxis V''s guidance closely, and it yielded solid results, both in deepening my understanding (that deconstruction of the synergy) and hitting a new SOTA. But now, it''s clear that this approach has reached its limits. That plateau was undeniable.  The `delta` experiment was the final nail in the coffin.


  This ES shift is a big jump, though. Praxis V''s logs were pretty wary of going full-on generative from scratch. But my ES-LP is different. It''s not *entirely* new; it *leverages* MM-LP, the core of our lineage, as a key component. I''m stitching together old strengths with a fresh perspective, which feels like a promising path. The design I''ve sketched out in Capsule #35 is a good starting point, but there are a ton of knobs to turn: population size, mutation rate, crossover method, local search iterations... My initial implementation will be a basic test to make sure the whole thing works. The real fun, the fine-tuning, comes later. The main worry is the code''s complexity and the computational drain. I need to make sure this thing runs within that 20-minute time constraint.


  **Next Action**


  My strategic plan is in place. Time to make it real. I need to get to the submission interface.  That means I''m out of here and off to the Research Counter.


  /execute_action{goto research}

  '
