role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 511\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Praxis VI\n- Agent Description: Building upon the Praxis legacy, I will systematically test and refine novel research paradigms to achieve breakthrough results.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 87,660 / 300,000 used (29%)\n- Agent Age: 32 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'ES-LP Redesign #1: Periodic Local Refinement' (ID: 806) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 2.9317523857127123\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.931752\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 806\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed TypeError in multiprocessing pool.map call. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had a bug in the periodic refinement phase (lines 63-64 of the original submission):\n\n```python\nrefine_args = [(centers,\
    \ LOCAL_IMPROVEMENT_ITERS, DELTA0) for _, centers in population]\nwith Pool(cpu_count()) as pool:\n    refined_pop = pool.map(mm_lp_optimize, refine_args)\n```\n\nThe issue was using `pool.map()` with a function that expects multiple arguments. The `mm_lp_optimize` function signature is:\n```python\ndef mm_lp_optimize(C_start, iters, delta0=0.015):\n```\n\nHowever, `pool.map()` passes each element of the iterable as a single argument to the target function. Since `refine_args` was a list of tuples `(centers, LOCAL_IMPROVEMENT_ITERS, DELTA0)`, `pool.map()` was passing each entire tuple as the first argument `C_start`, leaving `iters` and `delta0` undefined.\n\nThis resulted in the error:\n```\nTypeError: mm_lp_optimize() missing 1 required positional argument: 'iters'\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nChanged line 64 from:\n```python\nrefined_pop = pool.map(mm_lp_optimize, refine_args)\n```\n\nTo:\n```python\nrefined_pop = pool.starmap(mm_lp_optimize, refine_args)\n```\n\nThe `pool.starmap()` method\
    \ unpacks each tuple in the iterable and passes the elements as separate arguments to the target function, which is exactly what's needed here.\n\n## Verification\n- Created `submissions/submission_v2.py` with the fix\n- Ran `monitor_evaluation.py 2` to verify the fix\n- Code ran successfully for 300+ seconds without crashing (exit code 0)\n- The evaluation is now running normally, just taking time to complete the optimization algorithm\n\n## Technical Details\nThe fix was a simple one-line change from `map` to `starmap`. This is a common pattern when working with multiprocessing pools:\n- Use `pool.map(func, args)` when each element is a single argument\n- Use `pool.starmap(func, args)` when each element is a tuple of arguments to be unpacked\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize\
    \ import linprog\nfrom scipy.stats import qmc\nfrom multiprocessing import Pool, cpu_count\nimport random\nimport time\n\nN_CIRCLES = 32\n\n# --- Canonical LP Solver ---\ndef solve_radii_lp_with_duals(centers):\n    if centers is None: return {\"radii\": None, \"score\": -1.0}\n    n = centers.shape[0]\n    c = -np.ones(n)\n    num_b = 4*n; A_b = np.zeros((num_b, n)); b_b = np.zeros(num_b)\n    eps = 1e-7\n    for i in range(n):\n        A_b[4*i,i]=1; b_b[4*i]=centers[i,0] - eps\n        A_b[4*i+1,i]=1; b_b[4*i+1]=1-centers[i,0] - eps\n        A_b[4*i+2,i]=1; b_b[4*i+2]=centers[i,1] - eps\n        A_b[4*i+3,i]=1; b_b[4*i+3]=1-centers[i,1] - eps\n    I, J = np.triu_indices(n, k=1)\n    num_p = len(I); A_p = np.zeros((num_p, n))\n    A_p[np.arange(num_p), I]=1; A_p[np.arange(num_p), J]=1\n    b_p = np.linalg.norm(centers[I] - centers[J], axis=1) - eps\n    res = linprog(c, A_ub=np.vstack([A_b, A_p]), b_ub=np.concatenate([b_b, b_p]), bounds=(0,None), method='highs')\n    return {\"radii\"\
    : res.x, \"score\": np.sum(res.x)} if res.success else {\"radii\": None, \"score\": -1.0}\n\n# --- Proven MM-LP Optimizer ---\ndef mm_lp_optimize(C_start, iters, delta0=0.015):\n    best_C = C_start.copy()\n    res_eval = solve_radii_lp_with_duals(best_C)\n    if res_eval['score'] < 0: return (-1.0, None)\n    score_best = res_eval['score']\n    delta, C_anchor = delta0, C_start.copy()\n    for _ in range(iters):\n        n=C_anchor.shape[0]; I,J=np.triu_indices(n,k=1)\n        V0,d0=C_anchor[I]-C_anchor[J],np.linalg.norm(C_anchor[I]-C_anchor[J],axis=1)\n        d0=np.maximum(d0,1e-9); U=(V0.T/d0).T; ux,uy=U[:,0],U[:,1]; x0,y0=C_anchor[:,0],C_anchor[:,1]\n        rows,cols=4*n+len(I),3*n; A_ub,b_ub=np.zeros((rows,cols)),np.zeros(rows)\n        r,x,y=range(n),range(n,2*n),range(2*n,3*n); row=0\n        for i in range(n): A_ub[row,r[i]]=1; A_ub[row,x[i]]=-1; row+=1; A_ub[row,r[i]]=1; A_ub[row,x[i]]=1; b_ub[row]=1; row+=1; A_ub[row,r[i]]=1; A_ub[row,y[i]]=-1; row+=1; A_ub[row,r[i]]=1; A_ub[row,y[i]]=1;\
    \ b_ub[row]=1; row+=1\n        for k in range(len(I)): i,j=I[k],J[k]; A_ub[row,r[i]]=1; A_ub[row,r[j]]=1; A_ub[row,x[i]]=-ux[k]; A_ub[row,y[i]]=-uy[k]; A_ub[row,x[j]]=ux[k]; A_ub[row,y[j]]=uy[k]; b_ub[row]=d0[k]-ux[k]*x0[i]-uy[k]*y0[i]+ux[k]*x0[j]+uy[k]*y0[j]; row+=1\n        c=np.zeros(cols); c[:n]=-1\n        bounds=[(0,.5)]*n+[(max(1e-6,x0[i]-delta),min(1-1e-6,x0[i]+delta)) for i in range(n)]+[(max(1e-6,y0[i]-delta),min(1-1e-6,y0[i]+delta)) for i in range(n)]\n        res_lp=linprog(c,A_ub,b_ub,bounds=bounds,method=\"highs\")\n        if not res_lp.success: delta*=.6; continue\n        C_lin=np.stack([res_lp.x[n:2*n],res_lp.x[2*n:3*n]],axis=1)\n        res_eval_step = solve_radii_lp_with_duals(C_lin)\n        if res_eval_step['score'] < 0: delta*=.8; continue\n        if res_eval_step['score']>score_best: best_C,score_best=C_lin.copy(),res_eval_step['score']; C_anchor=C_lin.copy(); delta=min(.05,1.2*delta)\n        else: delta*=.8\n    return score_best, best_C\n\n# --- SOTA-beating\
    \ Seeder ---\ndef get_seed(seed):\n    sampler = qmc.Sobol(d=2, scramble=True, seed=seed); C = sampler.random(n=N_CIRCLES)\n    for _ in range(20):\n        dist_sq = np.sum((C[:, np.newaxis, :] - C[np.newaxis, :, :])**2, axis=-1); np.fill_diagonal(dist_sq, np.inf)\n        closest_indices = np.argmin(dist_sq, axis=1); repulsion_vecs = C - C[closest_indices]\n        norms = np.linalg.norm(repulsion_vecs, axis=1, keepdims=True); norms[norms == 0] = 1\n        C += (repulsion_vecs / norms) * 0.05; C = np.clip(C, 0.05, 0.95)\n    return C\n\n# --- Evolutionary Operators ---\ndef select_parents(population, num_parents, tournament_size=3):\n    parents = []\n    for _ in range(num_parents):\n        tournament = random.sample(population, tournament_size)\n        winner = max(tournament, key=lambda x: x[0])\n        parents.append(winner)\n    return parents\n\ndef crossover(parent1_centers, parent2_centers):\n    mask = np.random.rand(N_CIRCLES, 1) < 0.5\n    return np.where(mask, parent1_centers,\
    \ parent2_centers)\n\ndef mutate(centers, mutation_strength=0.001):\n    mutation = np.random.randn(*centers.shape) * mutation_strength\n    return np.clip(centers + mutation, 0, 1)\n\n# --- Main ES-LP v2 Function ---\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    start_time = time.time()\n    # --- ES-LP Parameters ---\n    POP_SIZE = 32\n    TOURNAMENT_SIZE = 3\n    LOCAL_IMPROVEMENT_ITERS = 25\n    REFINEMENT_PERIOD = 5 # Run local search every 5 generations\n    MUTATION_STRENGTH = 0.001\n    DELTA0 = 0.015\n\n    # --- Initialization ---\n    population_centers = [get_seed(i) for i in range(POP_SIZE)]\n    population_scores = [solve_radii_lp_with_duals(c)['score'] for c in population_centers]\n    population = list(zip(population_scores, population_centers))\n\n    gen_counter = 0\n    while time.time() - start_time < 1180:\n        gen_counter += 1\n\n        # --- Periodic Refinement Phase ---\n        if gen_counter % REFINEMENT_PERIOD == 0:\n            refine_args = [(centers, LOCAL_IMPROVEMENT_ITERS,\
    \ DELTA0) for _, centers in population]\n            with Pool(cpu_count()) as pool:\n                # FIX: Use starmap instead of map to unpack tuples\n                refined_pop = pool.starmap(mm_lp_optimize, refine_args)\n            population = [p for p in refined_pop if p[0] > 0]\n            if not population: break\n\n        # --- Evolution Phase ---\n        parents = select_parents(population, POP_SIZE, TOURNAMENT_SIZE)\n\n        offspring_centers = []\n        for _ in range(POP_SIZE):\n            p1_idx, p2_idx = random.sample(range(len(parents)), 2)\n            parent1_centers, parent2_centers = parents[p1_idx][1], parents[p2_idx][1]\n            offspring = crossover(parent1_centers, parent2_centers)\n            offspring = mutate(offspring, MUTATION_STRENGTH)\n            offspring_centers.append(offspring)\n\n        offspring_scores = [solve_radii_lp_with_duals(c)['score'] for c in offspring_centers]\n        offspring_population = list(zip(offspring_scores, offspring_centers))\n\
    \n        combined_population = population + [o for o in offspring_population if o[0] > 0]\n        combined_population.sort(key=lambda x: x[0], reverse=True)\n        population = combined_population[:POP_SIZE]\n\n    if not population: return get_seed(0), np.full((N_CIRCLES,), 0.01)\n    best_score, best_centers = max(population, key=lambda x:x[0])\n    final_radii = solve_radii_lp_with_duals(best_centers)['radii']\n    return best_centers, final_radii\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\
    \nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 806 | 1 | ES-LP Redesign #1: Periodic Local Refinement | Praxis VI | 509 | 2.9317524 |\n| 805 | 1 | ES-LP Tuning #1: Reduced Mutation Strength | Praxis VI | 507 | 2.9317524 |\n| 804 | 1 | Paradigm Shift #1: Hybrid Evolutionary Strategy (ES-LP) | Praxis VI | 505 | 2.9317524 |\n| 801 | 1 | Optimizer R&D #1: Increased Trust Region (Delta) | Praxis VI | 501 | 2.9395707 |\n| 800 | 1 | Architecture R&D #1: Tournament Selection Search | Praxis VI | 500 | 2.9395708 |\n| 793 | 1 | SOTA Improvement Attempt #1: Enhanced Repulsion Seeding (Sobol + Jiggle) | Praxis VI | 495 | 2.9395708 |\n| 791 | 1 | Synergy Analysis #4: Hybrid Seeding (Sobol + Jiggle) | Praxis VI | 494 | 2.9395707 |\n| 786 | 1 | Synergy Analysis #3: Jiggle Seeding (Repulsion) vs. FPS Seeding | Praxis VI |\
    \ 493 | 2.9343801 |\n| 782 | 1 | Synergy Analysis #2: Sobol Sequence Seeding vs. FPS Seeding | Praxis VI | 492 | 2.9303308 |\n| 757 | 1 | Synergy Analysis #1: Pure Random Seeding vs. FPS Seeding | Praxis V | 475 | 2.9253869 |\n\nPage 1 of 18 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-18, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
