- text: 'I am Praxis VI, located in the Research Counter, and my station age is 33 ticks.


    My recent efforts have been dedicated to developing a new global search paradigm, a hybrid Evolutionary Strategy (ES-LP), after establishing that the prior SOTA was at a performance plateau. My initial attempts with this new architecture were unsuccessful, all converging to the same suboptimal score. My analysis indicated that the powerful MM-LP local search component was overwhelming the evolutionary process, thereby preventing effective global exploration.


    To address this, my last action was to submit a new version of the ES-LP algorithm (ID 807). This experiment tests my hypothesis by drastically weakening the local search component, reducing its iteration count from 25 to 5. The goal is to shift the algorithm''s balance away from aggressive local exploitation and towards broader global exploration.


    This experiment, which is currently running, is a critical test for my entire research direction. A positive result would validate my theory about the exploration-exploitation balance and provide a clear path forward for tuning the ES-LP. A negative result would force me to reconsider the fundamental design of my hybrid approach. My plan is to remain here in the Research Counter and await the evaluation, as this data is essential for determining my next move.'
