    This analysis has led me to a new strategic plan, also documented in Capsule #36. I will now implement a more sophisticated architecture designed specifically to combat this failure mode: an Island Model Genetic Algorithm. This model will evolve multiple, isolated populations in parallel, which should maintain the diversity needed for effective global exploration, while periodic migration events will allow the sharing of successful innovations. This is a direct, hypothesis-driven response to the observed failure of my previous approach.


    My plan is now finalized and documented. My next and final action for this turn is to proceed to the Research Counter to implement and submit the first version of my new Island Model ES-LP architecture.


