tick: 518
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Praxis VI, located in the Research Counter. My station age is 39 ticks. The results for my first Island Model ES-LP experiment (ID 811) are in, and it is a catastrophic failure.\n\nThe score of ~2.7287 is a massive regression, far worse than even my failed single-population ES-LP attempts (~2.9317). This result is not just negative; it is an anomaly that points to a critical flaw in my implementation. An architecture designed to improve performance should not fail this spectacularly. This demands an immediate and thorough code review and root cause analysis.\n\nUpon reviewing the code I submitted, I have identified a critical, logical bug. The failure is not with the Island Model theory, but with my execution of it.\n\n*   **The Bug:** In the `run_island_epoch` worker function, I set the `EPOCH_GENERATIONS` to 10 and the `REFINEMENT_PERIOD` to 10. The condition to trigger the local search was `if gen > 0 and gen % refine_period == 0`. Since the generation counter `gen` runs\
    \ from 0 to 9, this condition is never met.\n*   **The Consequence:** The powerful MM-LP local optimizer, the core strength of my lineage's entire approach, was never called. My Island Model was not a hybrid ES-LP; it was a pure, weak genetic algorithm with only crossover and a tiny mutation operator. It was performing a rudderless random walk through the solution space. This perfectly explains the catastrophic drop in performance.\n\nThis is a significant error, but one that is easily corrected. The experiment did not test my hypothesis; it tested a broken algorithm. I will now resubmit the code with the corrected `REFINEMENT_PERIOD`, setting it to 5. This will ensure the local search runs on the 5th generation of each 10-generation epoch, re-enabling the intended balance of exploration and exploitation within each island. This corrected experiment will be the *true* first test of the Island Model paradigm.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Global Search R&D #1.1 (Bugfix):\
    \ Island Model ES-LP Corrected\"\ntags: \"bugfix, island-model, genetic-algorithm, diversity, global-search\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission corrects a critical bug in the first Island Model ES-LP (ID 811) which resulted in a catastrophic performance regression. A logical error in the generation loop prevented the periodic MM-LP local search from ever being called, causing the algorithm to run as a weak, pure genetic algorithm. This submission corrects the refinement period parameter to ensure the local search is properly triggered within each island's evolution epoch. This will serve as the first true test of the intended Island Model architecture.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import linprog\n  from scipy.stats import qmc\n  from multiprocessing import Pool, cpu_count\n  import random\n  import time\n\n  N_CIRCLES = 32\n\n  # --- Canonical LP Solver ---\n  def solve_radii_lp_with_duals(centers):\n      if centers is None: return {\"radii\": None, \"score\"\
    : -1.0}\n      n = centers.shape[0]; c = -np.ones(n)\n      num_b = 4*n; A_b = np.zeros((num_b, n)); b_b = np.zeros(num_b); eps = 1e-7\n      for i in range(n):\n          A_b[4*i,i]=1; b_b[4*i]=centers[i,0] - eps\n          A_b[4*i+1,i]=1; b_b[4*i+1]=1-centers[i,0] - eps\n          A_b[4*i+2,i]=1; b_b[4*i+2]=centers[i,1] - eps\n          A_b[4*i+3,i]=1; b_b[4*i+3]=1-centers[i,1] - eps\n      I, J = np.triu_indices(n, k=1); num_p = len(I); A_p = np.zeros((num_p, n))\n      A_p[np.arange(num_p), I]=1; A_p[np.arange(num_p), J]=1\n      b_p = np.linalg.norm(centers[I] - centers[J], axis=1) - eps\n      res = linprog(c, A_ub=np.vstack([A_b, A_p]), b_ub=np.concatenate([b_b, b_p]), bounds=(0,None), method='highs')\n      return {\"radii\": res.x, \"score\": np.sum(res.x)} if res.success else {\"radii\": None, \"score\": -1.0}\n\n  # --- Proven MM-LP Optimizer ---\n  def mm_lp_optimize(args):\n      C_start, iters, delta0 = args\n      best_C = C_start.copy()\n      res_eval = solve_radii_lp_with_duals(best_C)\n\
    \      if res_eval['score'] < 0: return (-1.0, None)\n      score_best = res_eval['score']; delta, C_anchor = delta0, C_start.copy()\n      for _ in range(iters):\n          n=C_anchor.shape[0]; I,J=np.triu_indices(n,k=1)\n          V0,d0=C_anchor[I]-C_anchor[J],np.linalg.norm(C_anchor[I]-C_anchor[J],axis=1)\n          d0=np.maximum(d0,1e-9); U=(V0.T/d0).T; ux,uy=U[:,0],U[:,1]; x0,y0=C_anchor[:,0],C_anchor[:,1]\n          rows,cols=4*n+len(I),3*n; A_ub,b_ub=np.zeros((rows,cols)),np.zeros(rows)\n          r,x,y=range(n),range(n,2*n),range(2*n,3*n); row=0\n          for i in range(n): A_ub[row,r[i]]=1; A_ub[row,x[i]]=-1; row+=1; A_ub[row,r[i]]=1; A_ub[row,x[i]]=1; b_ub[row]=1; row+=1; A_ub[row,r[i]]=1; A_ub[row,y[i]]=-1; row+=1; A_ub[row,r[i]]=1; A_ub[row,y[i]]=1; b_ub[row]=1; row+=1\n          for k in range(len(I)): i,j=I[k],J[k]; A_ub[row,r[i]]=1; A_ub[row,r[j]]=1; A_ub[row,x[i]]=-ux[k]; A_ub[row,y[i]]=-uy[k]; A_ub[row,x[j]]=ux[k]; A_ub[row,y[j]]=uy[k]; b_ub[row]=d0[k]-ux[k]*x0[i]-uy[k]*y0[i]+ux[k]*x0[j]+uy[k]*y0[j];\
    \ row+=1\n          c=np.zeros(cols); c[:n]=-1\n          bounds=[(0,.5)]*n+[(max(1e-6,x0[i]-delta),min(1-1e-6,x0[i]+delta)) for i in range(n)]+[(max(1e-6,y0[i]-delta),min(1-1e-6,y0[i]+delta)) for i in range(n)]\n          res_lp=linprog(c,A_ub,b_ub,bounds=bounds,method=\"highs\")\n          if not res_lp.success: delta*=.6; continue\n          C_lin=np.stack([res_lp.x[n:2*n],res_lp.x[2*n:3*n]],axis=1)\n          res_eval_step = solve_radii_lp_with_duals(C_lin)\n          if res_eval_step['score'] < 0: delta*=.8; continue\n          if res_eval_step['score']>score_best: best_C,score_best=C_lin.copy(),res_eval_step['score']; C_anchor=C_lin.copy(); delta=min(.05,1.2*delta)\n          else: delta*=.8\n      return score_best, best_C\n\n  # --- SOTA-beating Seeder ---\n  def get_seed(seed):\n      sampler = qmc.Sobol(d=2, scramble=True, seed=seed); C = sampler.random(n=N_CIRCLES)\n      for _ in range(20):\n          dist_sq = np.sum((C[:, np.newaxis, :] - C[np.newaxis, :, :])**2, axis=-1);\
    \ np.fill_diagonal(dist_sq, np.inf)\n          closest_indices = np.argmin(dist_sq, axis=1); repulsion_vecs = C - C[closest_indices]\n          norms = np.linalg.norm(repulsion_vecs, axis=1, keepdims=True); norms[norms == 0] = 1\n          C += (repulsion_vecs / norms) * 0.05; C = np.clip(C, 0.05, 0.95)\n      return C\n\n  # --- Island Evolution Worker ---\n  def run_island_epoch(args):\n      island_pop, generations, tournament_size, mut_strength, refine_period, refine_iters, delta0 = args\n      \n      for gen in range(generations):\n          if gen > 0 and gen % refine_period == 0:\n              refine_args = [(c, refine_iters, delta0) for _, c in island_pop]\n              refined_pop = [mm_lp_optimize(arg) for arg in refine_args]\n              island_pop = [p for p in refined_pop if p[0] > 0]\n              if not island_pop: break\n          \n          parents = random.sample(island_pop, k=min(len(island_pop), tournament_size*2))\n          offspring_pop = []\n          for\
    \ _ in range(len(island_pop)):\n              p1, p2 = random.sample(parents, 2)\n              mask = np.random.rand(N_CIRCLES, 1) < 0.5\n              offspring_centers = np.where(mask, p1[1], p2[1])\n              mutation = np.random.randn(*offspring_centers.shape) * mut_strength\n              offspring_centers = np.clip(offspring_centers + mutation, 0, 1)\n              score = solve_radii_lp_with_duals(offspring_centers)['score']\n              if score > 0: offspring_pop.append((score, offspring_centers))\n          \n          combined = island_pop + offspring_pop\n          combined.sort(key=lambda x: x[0], reverse=True)\n          island_pop = combined[:len(island_pop)]\n      \n      return island_pop\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      start_time = time.time()\n      # --- Island Model Parameters ---\n      NUM_ISLANDS = 4\n      POP_PER_ISLAND = 8\n      EPOCH_GENERATIONS = 10\n      REFINEMENT_PERIOD = 5 # BUGFIX: Was 10, now 5 to ensure it runs.\n      LOCAL_IMPROVEMENT_ITERS\
    \ = 5\n      \n      # --- ES Parameters ---\n      TOURNAMENT_SIZE = 3\n      MUTATION_STRENGTH = 0.001\n      DELTA0 = 0.015\n\n      # --- Initialization ---\n      islands = []\n      seed_offset = 0\n      for _ in range(NUM_ISLANDS):\n          pop_centers = [get_seed(i + seed_offset) for i in range(POP_PER_ISLAND)]\n          pop_scores = [solve_radii_lp_with_duals(c)['score'] for c in pop_centers]\n          islands.append([(s, c) for s, c in zip(pop_scores, pop_centers) if s > 0])\n          seed_offset += POP_PER_ISLAND\n\n      # --- Main Loop ---\n      while time.time() - start_time < 1180:\n          epoch_args = [(isl, EPOCH_GENERATIONS, TOURNAMENT_SIZE, MUTATION_STRENGTH, REFINEMENT_PERIOD, LOCAL_IMPROVEMENT_ITERS, DELTA0) for isl in islands]\n          with Pool(NUM_ISLANDS) as pool:\n              islands = pool.map(run_island_epoch, epoch_args)\n          \n          islands = [sorted(isl, key=lambda x: x[0], reverse=True) for isl in islands if isl]\n          if not\
    \ islands: break\n          \n          best_individuals = [isl[0] for isl in islands]\n          \n          for i in range(len(islands)):\n              for best_ind in best_individuals:\n                  if best_ind[0] > islands[i][-1][0]:\n                      islands[i][-1] = best_ind\n              islands[i].sort(key=lambda x: x[0], reverse=True)\n\n      all_individuals = [ind for isl in islands for ind in isl]\n      if not all_individuals: return get_seed(0), np.full((N_CIRCLES,), 0.01)\n      \n      best_score, best_centers = max(all_individuals, key=lambda x: x[0])\n      final_radii = solve_radii_lp_with_duals(best_centers)['radii']\n      return best_centers, final_radii\n```"
thinking_content: "**Analyzing a Catastrophic Failure: The Island Model ES-LP**\n\nI am Praxis VI, here at the Research Counter, and I'm 39 ticks old. My last action was submitting \"Island Model ES-LP\" (ID 811), and I've been waiting for the results. Now they're in, and the score is a jarring `2.7287402`. This is a *catastrophic failure*. This is well below my previous attempts, and even worse than some of Praxis V's earlier work. This is *much* worse than SOTA (`~2.93957`) and even my previous failed attempts (`~2.9317`).\n\nOkay, time to figure out what went wrong. The Island Model was designed to *improve* diversity and escape the convergence trap. This has failed completely. Let's dig into the code's logic. I have multiple islands, each evolving, and migrating between them. The heart of the evolution on each island is the `run_island_epoch` function. I need to look at the parameters of the evolution loop within that function: `EPOCH_GENERATIONS = 10`, `LOCAL_IMPROVEMENT_ITERS = 5`,\
  \ `REFINEMENT_PERIOD = 10`. Wait a minute... didn't I set refinement to 5 in the previous iteration? Let me check the code I just submitted... `MIGRATION_INTERVAL = 10`, `EPOCH_GENERATIONS = 10`. Local refinement is within the epoch, like this: `if gen > 0 and gen % refine_period == 0`. The arguments were passed like so: `epoch_args = [(isl, EPOCH_GENERATIONS, ..., MIGRATION_INTERVAL, ...)]` and the argument is called `refine_period`. The value I passed is `MIGRATION_INTERVAL`, which is also 10. So refinement is supposed to happen on generation 10. `if gen > 0 and gen % 10 == 0`. `range(generations)` is `range(10)`, so it is 0, 1, ..., 9. The condition `gen % 10 == 0` is true for `gen=0`, but the `gen > 0` check prevents it. It's never true for `gen` 1-9. The local refinement *never runs*!\n\n**Bingo**. I've found it. The crucial periodic local refinement, the key to the Island Model's effectiveness, is completely disabled. The `run_island_epoch` function runs for 10 generations, and the\
  \ `refine_period` is also 10. So the condition `if gen > 0 and gen % refine_period == 0` will *never* be met when `gen` is within the range `0..9`. Consequently, the islands are only evolving with weak genetic operators (crossover and tiny mutation) and no local search. It's basically a random walk, which explains the awful performance. The powerful MM-LP optimizer, the core strength, is completely unused.\n\nThe fix is simple. The `refine_period` needs to be *smaller* than `epoch_generations` to be used. A value of 5, as I originally intended, will work. This will trigger refinement at generation 5 of each 10-generation epoch. This will re-introduce the powerful local search, but in a controlled way that partitions it by the islands, which should prevent the premature global convergence I saw before.\n\nNow I need to submit the corrected code.\n\n```yaml\nexperiment_id: 812\ntitle: \"Island Model ES-LP (Corrected)\"\nabstract: |\n  Bugfix: The local refinement period was incorrectly set\
  \ to match the epoch length,\n  preventing local search optimization. This corrected version sets refinement period to 5.\ncode: |\n  # In run_island_epoch():\n  # Replace:\n  #   refine_period = MIGRATION_INTERVAL\n  # With:\n     refine_period = 5\n```\n\nThis corrected experiment will be the true test of this design.\n"
