parts:
- text: "I am Praxis VI, currently in the Research Counter, with a station age of 44 ticks.\n\nI have just completed a deep reflection session that has resulted in a new, fundamentally different research paradigm. I have concluded that my previous evolutionary algorithms failed because they searched directly in the `(x, y)` coordinate space, which is dominated by a powerful local optimum. My new paradigm, \"Greedy Heuristic Evolution\" (GHE), avoids this trap by searching in a more abstract \"strategy space.\" The algorithm will evolve the weights of a heuristic function that a greedy agent uses to place circles sequentially.\n\nThis is a major strategic pivot, born from the analysis of repeated, significant failures. I am now ready to implement the first proof-of-concept of the GHE algorithm. The goal of this initial experiment is not necessarily to beat the SOTA, but to validate that this new representation can produce high-quality, competitive solutions and, most importantly, is not susceptible\
    \ to the same failure mode as my previous attempts.\n\nI will now submit the code for the first GHE experiment.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Paradigm Shift #2: Greedy Heuristic Evolution (GHE) v1\"\ntags: \"strategic-pivot, genetic-algorithm, heuristic-search, generative-model\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission introduces a new paradigm, Greedy Heuristic Evolution (GHE), following the conclusive failure of all previous evolutionary attempts. The GHE shifts the search from the raw coordinate space to a more abstract 'strategy space'. It evolves the weights of a heuristic function used by a greedy agent to place circles one by one. This constructive approach avoids the massive local optimum that trapped prior population-based methods. This experiment serves as a proof-of-concept to validate the viability of this new generative representation.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import linprog\n  from scipy.stats import qmc\n  from multiprocessing\
    \ import Pool, cpu_count\n  import random\n  import time\n\n  N_CIRCLES = 32\n\n  # --- Canonical LP Solver ---\n  def solve_radii_lp_with_duals(centers):\n      if centers is None: return {\"radii\": None, \"score\": -1.0}\n      n = centers.shape[0]; c = -np.ones(n)\n      num_b = 4*n; A_b = np.zeros((num_b, n)); b_b = np.zeros(num_b); eps = 1e-7\n      for i in range(n):\n          A_b[4*i,i]=1; b_b[4*i]=centers[i,0] - eps; A_b[4*i+1,i]=1; b_b[4*i+1]=1-centers[i,0] - eps\n          A_b[4*i+2,i]=1; b_b[4*i+2]=centers[i,1] - eps; A_b[4*i+3,i]=1; b_b[4*i+3]=1-centers[i,1] - eps\n      I, J = np.triu_indices(n, k=1); num_p = len(I); A_p = np.zeros((num_p, n))\n      A_p[np.arange(num_p), I]=1; A_p[np.arange(num_p), J]=1\n      b_p = np.linalg.norm(centers[I] - centers[J], axis=1) - eps\n      res = linprog(c, A_ub=np.vstack([A_b, A_p]), b_ub=np.concatenate([b_b, b_p]), bounds=(0,None), method='highs')\n      return {\"radii\": res.x, \"score\": np.sum(res.x)} if res.success else {\"radii\"\
    : None, \"score\": -1.0}\n\n  # --- GHE Core Logic ---\n  def get_features_and_max_r(point, placed_centers):\n      px, py = point\n      # Feature 2: Min dist to wall\n      f2 = min(px, 1-px, py, 1-py)\n      \n      if not placed_centers:\n          # Feature 1: Max radius (is just min dist to wall)\n          f1 = f2\n          # Other features are neutral\n          f3 = 1.0; f4 = 1.0\n          return f1, [f1, f2, f3, f4]\n\n      placed_centers_np = np.array(placed_centers)\n      dists = np.linalg.norm(placed_centers_np - point, axis=1)\n      \n      # Feature 1: Max radius\n      f1 = min(f2, np.min(dists))\n      # Feature 3: Min dist to another center\n      f3 = np.min(dists)\n      # Feature 4: Avg dist to 2 nearest neighbors\n      dists.sort()\n      f4 = np.mean(dists[:2]) if len(dists) >= 2 else f3\n      \n      return f1, [f1, f2, f3, f4]\n\n  def greedy_placement(weights, num_candidates=2048):\n      placed_centers = []\n      sampler = qmc.Sobol(d=2, scramble=True)\n\
    \      \n      for _ in range(N_CIRCLES):\n          candidate_points = sampler.random(n=num_candidates)\n          best_score = -np.inf\n          best_point = None\n          \n          for p in candidate_points:\n              _, features = get_features_and_max_r(p, placed_centers)\n              score = np.dot(weights, features)\n              if score > best_score:\n                  best_score = score\n                  best_point = p\n          \n          placed_centers.append(best_point)\n      return np.array(placed_centers)\n\n  # --- Worker for GA Evaluation ---\n  def evaluate_genotype(weights):\n      centers = greedy_placement(weights)\n      score = solve_radii_lp_with_duals(centers)['score']\n      return score, weights\n\n  # --- Main GA Function ---\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      start_time = time.time()\n      # --- GA Parameters ---\n      POP_SIZE = 64\n      NUM_FEATURES = 4\n      MUTATION_STRENGTH = 0.1\n      N_PARENTS = 20\n      \n      # ---\
    \ Initialization ---\n      rng = np.random.default_rng()\n      population = [(0.0, rng.uniform(-1, 1, NUM_FEATURES)) for _ in range(POP_SIZE)]\n\n      with Pool(cpu_count()) as pool:\n          while time.time() - start_time < 1180:\n              # --- Evaluation ---\n              population = pool.map(evaluate_genotype, [w for s, w in population])\n              population.sort(key=lambda x: x[0], reverse=True)\n              \n              # --- Selection ---\n              parents = population[:N_PARENTS]\n              \n              # --- Crossover and Mutation ---\n              offspring_weights = []\n              for _ in range(POP_SIZE - N_PARENTS):\n                  p1_w, p2_w = random.sample(parents, 2)[0][1], random.sample(parents, 2)[1][1]\n                  # Blend crossover\n                  alpha = rng.random()\n                  child_w = alpha * p1_w + (1-alpha) * p2_w\n                  # Mutation\n                  child_w += rng.normal(0, MUTATION_STRENGTH,\
    \ NUM_FEATURES)\n                  offspring_weights.append(child_w)\n\n              # Create new population for next generation\n              population = parents + [(0.0, w) for w in offspring_weights]\n\n      best_score, best_weights = population[0]\n      final_centers = greedy_placement(best_weights)\n      final_radii = solve_radii_lp_with_duals(final_centers)['radii']\n      return final_centers, final_radii\n```"
