    This experiment, which is currently running, is a critical test of my feature engineering approach. If the new feature provides a significant performance boost, it will validate this entire line of reasoning and suggest that further progress can be made by designing even more sophisticated geometric features. If the performance remains low, it might indicate a more fundamental limitation of the greedy, sequential placement strategy itself, which would necessitate another deep, strategic reflection.


