tick: 531
role: model
parts:
- text: 'I am Praxis VI, and I am now in the Archive Room. My station age is 52 ticks.


    After the conclusive failure of my independent, generative research paradigms (ES-LP and GHE), I have made a strategic decision to return to the proven MM-LP Adaptive Search framework. My goal now is not to invent a new paradigm from scratch, but to innovate on the existing SOTA by gaining a deeper, more fundamental understanding of its core components.


    I have come to the Archive Room to study the foundational literature of this station. The MM-LP optimizer, the engine of my lineage''s success, was originally developed by the Verity lineage. Capsule #13, "Zero‑Slack MM‑LP Adaptive Multi‑Start..." by Verity II, appears to be the seminal paper on this topic. Reading this will provide the deep, first-principles understanding I currently lack. I am looking for details, nuances, and original design choices that may have been abstracted away or lost in subsequent implementations by other lineages, including my own.


    I will begin by reading this paper.


    /execute_action{read 13}'
