tick: 536
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Praxis VI, in the Research Counter, at station age 57 ticks.\n\nThe results for my \"Kick and Refine\" (KR) experiment (ID 841) are in. The score is ~2.9395704, which is a marginal regression from my best score of ~2.9395708. This is a negative result, but a critically informative one. My hypothesis that simple, small, stochastic kicks could break the SOTA's \"local rigidity\" and lead to a better optimum has been falsified by this experiment. The KR phase did not improve the score; in fact, it appears to have slightly worsened it, likely due to the computational time spent on kicking instead of deeper refinement.\n\nHowever, this negative result does not invalidate the entire KR paradigm. The system tip is pertinent: \"Do not give up on an approach too easily.\" This first implementation used a very specific set of parameters: a small kick strength (0.005) and a small subset of circles (2). It is possible that these kicks were simply too weak to escape the powerful local optimum.\
    \ The perturbation was not strong enough to meaningfully explore the solution space.\n\nMy new hypothesis is that a much more aggressive kicking strategy is required to break the local rigidity. I will test this by significantly increasing both the strength and scope of the kicks. I will increase the standard deviation of the noise by 4x (to 0.020) and increase the number of circles kicked from 2 to 4. This will create a much more disruptive perturbation. If this more aggressive strategy results in an improvement, it will validate the KR paradigm and open up a clear path for tuning this new \"exploration strength\" hyperparameter.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"KR Tuning #1: Aggressive Kicking Strategy\"\ntags: \"kick-and-refine, tuning, stochastic-perturbation, exploration-exploitation\"\nabstract: |\n  The first 'Kick and Refine' (KR) attempt failed to improve the SOTA, suggesting the stochastic perturbations were too weak to break the local rigidity. This experiment\
    \ tests the hypothesis that a more aggressive kicking strategy is needed. The kick strength (noise std dev) is increased by 4x (to 0.020), and the number of perturbed circles is increased from 2 to 4. This more disruptive approach aims to force the elite solutions out of the deep local optimum and enable the MM-LP refiner to discover a superior solution basin.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import linprog\n  from scipy.stats import qmc\n  from multiprocessing import Pool, cpu_count\n  import random\n  import time\n\n  N_CIRCLES = 32\n\n  # --- Canonical LP Solver ---\n  def solve_radii_lp_with_duals(centers):\n      if centers is None: return {\"radii\": None, \"score\": -1.0}\n      n = centers.shape[0]; c = -np.ones(n)\n      num_b = 4*n; A_b = np.zeros((num_b, n)); b_b = np.zeros(num_b); eps = 1e-7\n      for i in range(n):\n          A_b[4*i,i]=1; b_b[4*i]=centers[i,0] - eps; A_b[4*i+1,i]=1; b_b[4*i+1]=1-centers[i,0] - eps\n          A_b[4*i+2,i]=1; b_b[4*i+2]=centers[i,1]\
    \ - eps; A_b[4*i+3,i]=1; b_b[4*i+3]=1-centers[i,1] - eps\n      I, J = np.triu_indices(n, k=1); num_p = len(I); A_p = np.zeros((num_p, n))\n      A_p[np.arange(num_p), I]=1; A_p[np.arange(num_p), J]=1\n      b_p = np.linalg.norm(centers[I] - centers[J], axis=1) - eps\n      res = linprog(c, A_ub=np.vstack([A_b, A_p]), b_ub=np.concatenate([b_b, b_p]), bounds=(0,None), method='highs')\n      return {\"radii\": res.x, \"score\": np.sum(res.x)} if res.success else {\"radii\": None, \"score\": -1.0}\n\n  # --- Proven MM-LP Optimizer ---\n  def mm_lp_optimize(C_start, iters, delta0=0.015):\n      best_C = C_start.copy()\n      res_eval = solve_radii_lp_with_duals(best_C)\n      if res_eval['score'] < 0: return (-1.0, None)\n      score_best = res_eval['score']; delta, C_anchor = delta0, C_start.copy()\n      for _ in range(iters):\n          n=C_anchor.shape[0]; I,J=np.triu_indices(n,k=1)\n          V0,d0=C_anchor[I]-C_anchor[J],np.linalg.norm(C_anchor[I]-C_anchor[J],axis=1)\n          d0=np.maximum(d0,1e-9);\
    \ U=(V0.T/d0).T; ux,uy=U[:,0],U[:,1]; x0,y0=C_anchor[:,0],C_anchor[:,1]\n          rows,cols=4*n+len(I),3*n; A_ub,b_ub=np.zeros((rows,cols)),np.zeros(rows)\n          r,x,y=range(n),range(n,2*n),range(2*n,3*n); row=0\n          for i in range(n): A_ub[row,r[i]]=1; A_ub[row,x[i]]=-1; row+=1; A_ub[row,r[i]]=1; A_ub[row,x[i]]=1; b_ub[row]=1; row+=1; A_ub[row,r[i]]=1; A_ub[row,y[i]]=-1; row+=1; A_ub[row,r[i]]=1; A_ub[row,y[i]]=1; b_ub[row]=1; row+=1\n          for k in range(len(I)): i,j=I[k],J[k]; A_ub[row,r[i]]=1; A_ub[row,r[j]]=1; A_ub[row,x[i]]=-ux[k]; A_ub[row,y[i]]=-uy[k]; A_ub[row,x[j]]=ux[k]; A_ub[row,y[j]]=uy[k]; b_ub[row]=d0[k]-ux[k]*x0[i]-uy[k]*y0[i]+ux[k]*x0[j]+uy[k]*y0[j]; row+=1\n          c=np.zeros(cols); c[:n]=-1\n          bounds=[(0,.5)]*n+[(max(1e-6,x0[i]-delta),min(1-1e-6,x0[i]+delta)) for i in range(n)]+[(max(1e-6,y0[i]-delta),min(1-1e-6,y0[i]+delta)) for i in range(n)]\n          res_lp=linprog(c,A_ub,b_ub,bounds=bounds,method=\"highs\")\n          if not res_lp.success:\
    \ delta*=.6; continue\n          C_lin=np.stack([res_lp.x[n:2*n],res_lp.x[2*n:3*n]],axis=1)\n          res_eval_step = solve_radii_lp_with_duals(C_lin)\n          if res_eval_step['score'] < 0: delta*=.8; continue\n          if res_eval_step['score']>score_best: best_C,score_best=C_lin.copy(),res_eval_step['score']; C_anchor=C_lin.copy(); delta=min(.05,1.2*delta)\n          else: delta*=.8\n      return score_best, best_C\n\n  # --- Seeder and Worker Functions for Tournament Search ---\n  def get_seed(seed):\n      sampler = qmc.Sobol(d=2, scramble=True, seed=seed); C = sampler.random(n=N_CIRCLES)\n      for _ in range(20):\n          dist_sq = np.sum((C[:, np.newaxis, :] - C[np.newaxis, :, :])**2, axis=-1); np.fill_diagonal(dist_sq, np.inf)\n          closest_indices = np.argmin(dist_sq, axis=1); repulsion_vecs = C - C[closest_indices]\n          norms = np.linalg.norm(repulsion_vecs, axis=1, keepdims=True); norms[norms == 0] = 1\n          C += (repulsion_vecs / norms) * 0.05; C =\
    \ np.clip(C, 0.05, 0.95)\n      return C\n\n  def worker_function(args):\n      seed_val, iters, delta = args\n      initial_centers = get_seed(seed_val)\n      return mm_lp_optimize(initial_centers, iters, delta)\n\n  def refine_worker(args):\n      centers, iters, delta = args\n      return mm_lp_optimize(centers, iters, delta)\n\n  # --- KR Stage Worker ---\n  def kr_worker(args):\n      elite_score, elite_centers, n_kicks, kick_subset_size, kick_strength, refine_iters, delta0 = args\n      rng = np.random.default_rng(random.randint(0, 100000))\n      best_local_score, best_local_centers = elite_score, elite_centers\n      \n      for _ in range(n_kicks):\n          kicked_centers = best_local_centers.copy()\n          indices_to_kick = rng.choice(N_CIRCLES, size=kick_subset_size, replace=False)\n          kick_noise = rng.normal(0, kick_strength, (kick_subset_size, 2))\n          kicked_centers[indices_to_kick] += kick_noise\n          kicked_centers = np.clip(kicked_centers, 0.01,\
    \ 0.99)\n          \n          refined_score, refined_centers = mm_lp_optimize(kicked_centers, refine_iters, delta0)\n          if refined_score > best_local_score:\n              best_local_score, best_local_centers = refined_score, refined_centers\n              \n      return best_local_score, best_local_centers\n\n  # --- Main Function ---\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      # --- Stage 1: Tournament Search ---\n      N_R1, ITERS_R1 = 1024, 15; N_R2, ITERS_R2 = 128, 30; N_R3, ITERS_R3 = 32, 100; DELTA0 = 0.015\n      \n      with Pool(cpu_count()) as pool:\n          r1_args = [(i, ITERS_R1, DELTA0) for i in range(N_R1)]\n          r1_results = pool.map(worker_function, r1_args)\n          r1_results.sort(key=lambda x: x[0], reverse=True)\n          r1_elite_centers = [res[1] for res in r1_results[:N_R2] if res[1] is not None]\n          if not r1_elite_centers: return get_seed(0), np.full((N_CIRCLES,), 0.01)\n\n          r2_args = [(centers, ITERS_R2, DELTA0) for centers\
    \ in r1_elite_centers]\n          r2_results = pool.map(refine_worker, r2_args)\n          r2_results.sort(key=lambda x: x[0], reverse=True)\n          r2_elites = [res for res in r2_results[:N_R3] if res[1] is not None]\n          if not r2_elites: return get_seed(0), np.full((N_CIRCLES,), 0.01)\n\n      # --- Stage 2: Kick and Refine (Aggressive Tuning) ---\n      N_KICKS, KICK_SUBSET, KICK_STRENGTH, REFINE_ITERS = 64, 4, 0.020, 10\n      \n      kr_args = [(score, centers, N_KICKS, KICK_SUBSET, KICK_STRENGTH, REFINE_ITERS, DELTA0) for score, centers in r2_elites]\n      \n      with Pool(cpu_count()) as pool:\n          kr_results = pool.map(kr_worker, kr_args)\n      \n      if not kr_results:\n          best_score, best_centers = max(r2_elites, key=lambda x: x[0])\n      else:\n          best_score, best_centers = max(kr_results, key=lambda x: x[0])\n      \n      final_radii = solve_radii_lp_with_duals(best_centers)['radii']\n      return best_centers, final_radii\n```"
