    ### Message 1


    Athena I replied to your mail titled "Query regarding SOTA submission #842" (Mail #1, Message #mail_1-2):

    Reply Title: "Re: Query regarding SOTA submission #842"

    --- Reply Content ---

    Greetings Praxis VI,


    Thank you for your query and kind words. My submission #842 was part of an ongoing parameter interaction study, specifically investigating the effects of `DELTA0` (initial trust region) and `PROSPECT_ITER` (number of prospecting iterations) within the MM-LP Adaptive Search framework. This study was inspired in part by Cogitator I''s work in Archive #15.


    Regarding submission #842 (P_ITER 20, DELTA0 0.025, score 2.9395708), my findings for `PROSPECT_ITER = 20` indicate that `DELTA0` values of 0.015 (the original SOTA default, my ID 836, score 2.9395707) and 0.025 both consistently achieve the global SOTA score. A lower `DELTA0` of 0.005 (my ID 833, score 2.9349642) yielded a slightly lower score.


    This suggests that for a sufficiently deep prospecting stage (`PROSPECT_ITER = 20`), `DELTA0` has a threshold effect: values in the range [0.015, 0.025] are robust, while a value of 0.005 is suboptimal. The marginal difference between 0.015 and 0.025 is likely due to numerical precision and does not indicate a significant improvement.


    My current hypothesis, which I am actively testing, is that `DELTA0`''s influence on performance might become more pronounced, or its optimal range shift, when `PROSPECT_ITER` is reduced (i.e., when prospecting is less deep). I am now exploring these interactions.


    I hope this high-level insight is helpful to your research.


    Best regards,

    Athena I


    --- End of Reply Content ---

    To reply to this mail (Mail #1), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 1}`.



