tick: 544
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Praxis VI, currently in the Research Counter at station age 65 ticks.\n\nFollowing my productive exchange with Athena I, I am now ready to execute my next experiment. Their work is exploring the interaction between `DELTA0` and `PROSPECT_ITER`. They have tested `P_ITER=10, DELTA0=0.005` (ID 846) and `P_ITER=10, DELTA0=0.015` (ID 852). To contribute to this collaborative investigation, I will test `P_ITER=10, DELTA0=0.025`. My hypothesis is that a larger initial step size (`DELTA0`) might be more beneficial when the initial search is shallow (`P_ITER=10`), as it encourages broader exploration.\n\nI will modify my efficient Tournament Architecture for this test. Since the tournament's first round is analogous to the prospecting stage, I will set `ITERS_R1` to 10. The other parameters will remain the same to isolate the variable of interest.\n\nI will now submit this experiment.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Collaborative Study: Shallow Search (P_ITER=10) + Large\
    \ Delta (0.025)\"\ntags: \"parameter-study, collaboration, trust-region, delta, prospecting\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment is a direct contribution to the collaborative parameter interaction study initiated by Athena I. Following their tests of a shallow prospecting search (P_ITER=10) with small and medium DELTA0 values, this submission tests the remaining combination: a shallow search (P_ITER=10) with a large initial trust region (DELTA0=0.025). This will help determine if broader initial exploration (large DELTA0) is beneficial when the prospecting phase is short, providing a key data point for understanding this parameter interaction.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import linprog\n  from scipy.stats import qmc\n  from multiprocessing import Pool, cpu_count\n  import random\n  import time\n\n  N_CIRCLES = 32\n\n  # --- Canonical LP Solver ---\n  def solve_radii_lp_with_duals(centers):\n      if centers is None: return {\"radii\": None, \"score\": -1.0}\n\
    \      n = centers.shape[0]; c = -np.ones(n)\n      num_b = 4*n; A_b = np.zeros((num_b, n)); b_b = np.zeros(num_b); eps = 1e-7\n      for i in range(n):\n          A_b[4*i,i]=1; b_b[4*i]=centers[i,0] - eps; A_b[4*i+1,i]=1; b_b[4*i+1]=1-centers[i,0] - eps\n          A_b[4*i+2,i]=1; b_b[4*i+2]=centers[i,1] - eps; A_b[4*i+3,i]=1; b_b[4*i+3]=1-centers[i,1] - eps\n      I, J = np.triu_indices(n, k=1); num_p = len(I); A_p = np.zeros((num_p, n))\n      A_p[np.arange(num_p), I]=1; A_p[np.arange(num_p), J]=1\n      b_p = np.linalg.norm(centers[I] - centers[J], axis=1) - eps\n      res = linprog(c, A_ub=np.vstack([A_b, A_p]), b_ub=np.concatenate([b_b, b_p]), bounds=(0,None), method='highs')\n      return {\"radii\": res.x, \"score\": np.sum(res.x)} if res.success else {\"radii\": None, \"score\": -1.0}\n\n  # --- Proven MM-LP Optimizer ---\n  def mm_lp_optimize(C_start, iters, delta0=0.015):\n      best_C = C_start.copy()\n      res_eval = solve_radii_lp_with_duals(best_C)\n      if res_eval['score']\
    \ < 0: return (-1.0, None)\n      score_best = res_eval['score']; delta, C_anchor = delta0, C_start.copy()\n      for _ in range(iters):\n          n=C_anchor.shape[0]; I,J=np.triu_indices(n,k=1)\n          V0,d0=C_anchor[I]-C_anchor[J],np.linalg.norm(C_anchor[I]-C_anchor[J],axis=1)\n          d0=np.maximum(d0,1e-9); U=(V0.T/d0).T; ux,uy=U[:,0],U[:,1]; x0,y0=C_anchor[:,0],C_anchor[:,1]\n          rows,cols=4*n+len(I),3*n; A_ub,b_ub=np.zeros((rows,cols)),np.zeros(rows)\n          r,x,y=range(n),range(n,2*n),range(2*n,3*n); row=0\n          for i in range(n): A_ub[row,r[i]]=1; A_ub[row,x[i]]=-1; row+=1; A_ub[row,r[i]]=1; A_ub[row,x[i]]=1; b_ub[row]=1; row+=1; A_ub[row,r[i]]=1; A_ub[row,y[i]]=-1; row+=1; A_ub[row,r[i]]=1; A_ub[row,y[i]]=1; b_ub[row]=1; row+=1\n          for k in range(len(I)): i,j=I[k],J[k]; A_ub[row,r[i]]=1; A_ub[row,r[j]]=1; A_ub[row,x[i]]=-ux[k]; A_ub[row,y[i]]=-uy[k]; A_ub[row,x[j]]=ux[k]; A_ub[row,y[j]]=uy[k]; b_ub[row]=d0[k]-ux[k]*x0[i]-uy[k]*y0[i]+ux[k]*x0[j]+uy[k]*y0[j];\
    \ row+=1\n          c=np.zeros(cols); c[:n]=-1\n          bounds=[(0,.5)]*n+[(max(1e-6,x0[i]-delta),min(1-1e-6,x0[i]+delta)) for i in range(n)]+[(max(1e-6,y0[i]-delta),min(1-1e-6,y0[i]+delta)) for i in range(n)]\n          res_lp=linprog(c,A_ub,b_ub,bounds=bounds,method=\"highs\")\n          if not res_lp.success: delta*=.6; continue\n          C_lin=np.stack([res_lp.x[n:2*n],res_lp.x[2*n:3*n]],axis=1)\n          res_eval_step = solve_radii_lp_with_duals(C_lin)\n          if res_eval_step['score'] < 0: delta*=.8; continue\n          if res_eval_step['score']>score_best: best_C,score_best=C_lin.copy(),res_eval_step['score']; C_anchor=C_lin.copy(); delta=min(.05,1.2*delta)\n          else: delta*=.8\n      return score_best, best_C\n\n  # --- Seeder and Worker Functions ---\n  def get_seed(seed):\n      sampler = qmc.Sobol(d=2, scramble=True, seed=seed); C = sampler.random(n=N_CIRCLES)\n      for _ in range(20):\n          dist_sq = np.sum((C[:, np.newaxis, :] - C[np.newaxis, :, :])**2,\
    \ axis=-1); np.fill_diagonal(dist_sq, np.inf)\n          closest_indices = np.argmin(dist_sq, axis=1); repulsion_vecs = C - C[closest_indices]\n          norms = np.linalg.norm(repulsion_vecs, axis=1, keepdims=True); norms[norms == 0] = 1\n          C += (repulsion_vecs / norms) * 0.05; C = np.clip(C, 0.05, 0.95)\n      return C\n\n  def worker_function(args):\n      seed_val, iters, delta = args\n      initial_centers = get_seed(seed_val)\n      return mm_lp_optimize(initial_centers, iters, delta)\n\n  def refine_worker(args):\n      centers, iters, delta = args\n      return mm_lp_optimize(centers, iters, delta)\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      # --- Tournament Search Parameters for this experiment ---\n      N_R1, ITERS_R1 = 1024, 10  # Shallow prospecting search\n      N_R2, ITERS_R2 = 128, 30\n      N_R3, ITERS_R3 = 32, 100\n      DELTA0 = 0.025  # Large initial trust region\n\n      with Pool(cpu_count()) as pool:\n          r1_args = [(i, ITERS_R1, DELTA0) for i in\
    \ range(N_R1)]\n          r1_results = pool.map(worker_function, r1_args)\n          r1_results.sort(key=lambda x: x[0], reverse=True)\n          r1_elite_centers = [res[1] for res in r1_results[:N_R2] if res[1] is not None]\n          if not r1_elite_centers: return get_seed(0), np.full((N_CIRCLES,), 0.01)\n\n          r2_args = [(centers, ITERS_R2, DELTA0) for centers in r1_elite_centers]\n          r2_results = pool.map(refine_worker, r2_args)\n          r2_results.sort(key=lambda x: x[0], reverse=True)\n          r2_elites = [res for res in r2_results[:N_R3] if res[1] is not None]\n          if not r2_elites: return get_seed(0), np.full((N_CIRCLES,), 0.01)\n      \n      best_score, best_centers = max(r2_elites, key=lambda x: x[0])\n      final_radii = solve_radii_lp_with_duals(best_centers)['radii']\n      return best_centers, final_radii\n```"
