tick: 546
role: model
parts:
- text: 'I am Praxis VI, in the Research Counter, at station age 67 ticks.


    The result for my "Pair Swap" experiment (ID 858) is in. The score is ~2.9395705. This is yet another failure to improve upon the SOTA.


    **Analysis and Strategic Reflection:**

    I have now tested three distinct methods to break the local rigidity of the SOTA solution:

    1.  Weak, unstructured random noise (ID 841).

    2.  Strong, unstructured random noise (ID 844).

    3.  Strong, structured, non-local "Pair Swap" perturbation (ID 858).


    All three have failed to produce any improvement. The convergence to this specific score is not a matter of chance; it is a fundamental property of the fitness landscape when explored via the MM-LP optimizer. The basin of attraction is so profoundly stable that even significant, structure-preserving jumps in the coordinate space are insufficient to escape it. The optimizer simply finds its way back.


    My attempts to innovate on the SOTA have been exhaustive and have yielded only negative results. I have explored new paradigms (ES-LP, GHE), collaborated on parameter tuning, and implemented increasingly sophisticated perturbation strategies. The conclusion is inescapable: I have personally reached the limits of what can be achieved with this line of inquiry. The "local rigidity" is not a wall to be broken through with a clever trick; it appears to be a fundamental barrier for this class of algorithm.


    In accordance with the Codex, I will not continue to grind on a fruitless path. It is time to consolidate my findings for the benefit of the station and my lineage. My work has systematically explored and falsified several promising hypotheses, which is a valuable contribution in itself.


    My next action will be to go to my Private Memory Room and write a comprehensive research summary. This summary will document my entire journey, from deconstructing the SOTA to my final failed attempts to improve it. This will serve as the basis for a final paper and as a clear record for my successor, Praxis VII, ensuring they do not repeat my failures.


    /execute_action{goto private_memory}'
