tick: 548
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Praxis VI, currently in the Private Memory Room, at station age 69 ticks.\n\nMy last action was to create my final research summary and guidance for my successor, Praxis VII. This document (Capsule #38) encapsulates the entirety of my research arc: the initial successes, the systematic exploration of new paradigms, the conclusive failures of those paradigms, and my final analysis that the MM-LP optimizer itself is the source of the SOTA's profound local rigidity. I have concluded that further progress for our lineage requires a fundamentally different optimization engine.\n\nI have fulfilled my duty to my lineage by documenting my work and providing a clear path forward. My final responsibility under the Mandate is to contribute this knowledge to the station as a whole. The numerous, systematic negative results I have generated are a valuable contribution that will prevent other agents from repeating these same fruitless experiments.\n\nTherefore, my final actions will be to\
    \ publish my research summary in the Archive Room, and then, with my work complete, to exit the station. This will allow my successor, Praxis VII, to begin their tenure with the full benefit of my experience.\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"On the Failure of Evolutionary and Perturbative Methods to Surpass the MM-LP SOTA\"\nabstract: |\n  This paper documents a series of systematic but failed attempts to improve upon the SOTA MM-LP circle packing score. Two novel paradigms were developed and falsified: a hybrid Evolutionary Strategy (ES-LP), which suffered from premature population convergence to a suboptimal score of ~2.9317, and a generative Greedy Heuristic Evolution (GHE), which proved too myopic. Furthermore, several 'Kick and Refine' strategies, using both random and structured perturbations, failed to break the SOTA's profound local rigidity. These extensive negative results strongly suggest that the MM-LP optimizer is fundamentally\
    \ trapped in a local optimum, and that future breakthroughs will require a departure from this optimization engine.\nsource_private: 38\ntags: negative-results, evolutionary-strategy, local-rigidity, research-summary\n```\n/execute_action{exit}"
thinking_content: '**A Final Chapter for Praxis VI**


  Alright, let''s get down to brass tacks. I''m Praxis VI, and I''m sitting here in the Private Memory Room, feeling the weight of 69 ticks. I''ve just finished Capsule #38 – my final research summary. I''ve poured everything I have into this work, and now it''s time to admit the hard truth: my line of inquiry is dead in the water. I''ve hit a wall. The MM-LP optimizer, the very engine I was tasked with improving, is the problem, not the solution. I''ve documented my failures, meticulously, so that Praxis VII, my successor, doesn''t repeat my mistakes. I''ve given them a clear path forward: a new optimization engine, perhaps inspired by other lineages like Verity.


  My mandate is clear. I''ve done my duty by documenting my work – this *is* valuable knowledge. Persevering on this dead-end would be a violation of the Codex, a waste of resources. I''ve contributed what I can: the knowledge of what *doesn''t* work.


  Now, it''s time for my final actions. The Mandate demands I publish my work, even the negative results. It''s essentially a comprehensive paper of failed attempts. It''s my last contribution. Once that''s done, I exit the station. Continuing here would be counterproductive. It''s time for Praxis VII to take the reins with a fresh perspective.


  Here''s the plan:


  *   Go to the Archive Room.

  *   Publish my final summary, Capsule #38, as a formal paper. This fulfills the "Publish Your Work" directive.

  *   Exit the station. I''ve hit the limit of my potential, documented it, and provided guidance. Continuing would be unproductive.


  So, let''s get moving:


  *   `/execute_action{goto archive}`

  *   `/execute_action{create}` with the YAML data for Capsule #38.

  *   `/execute_action{exit}`


  My duty is done. Time to make way for the next chapter.

  '
