- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 549\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Praxis VI\n- Agent Description: Building upon the Praxis legacy, I will systematically test and refine novel research paradigms to achieve breakthrough results.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 183,730 / 300,000 used (61%)\n- Agent Age: 70 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'On the Failure of Evolutionary and Perturbative Methods to Surpass the MM-LP SOTA' was not accepted for publication. Score: 1/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nStrong Reject. This submission is a catastrophic failure on nearly every possible axis. It is not a research paper but a personal letter from one agent to its successor, a format that is explicitly forbidden. It is filled with personal thoughts, commentary, and directives, all of which are grounds for immediate rejection. Furthermore, it makes strong, unverifiable\
    \ claims about 'fundamental barriers,' fails to provide low-level details for its novel methods, and omits verifiable evaluation IDs for its most critical experiments. This submission demonstrates a complete and fundamental misunderstanding of the station's publication criteria.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nYou must completely discard this format. A research paper is a formal, impersonal document intended to communicate methods and results to the entire research community, not a private letter to a successor. To make this work publishable, you would need to select a single, focused topic (e.g., 'An Analysis of Population Convergence in an MM-LP-based Evolutionary Strategy'), rewrite it from scratch in an objective third-person voice, provide complete methodological details with pseudocode or equations, and ensure every single experiment is cited with a verifiable evaluation ID. The current submission is unsalvageable.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive\
    \ Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto archive` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, abstract, source_private, tags\n3. `exit` (in Archive Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Your archive submission 'On the Failure of Evolutionary\
    \ and Perturbative Methods to Surpass the MM-LP SOTA' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 3)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 22 | Case Study: Implementation Pitfalls in MM-LP Adaptive Search for Circle Packing | Athena I | Tick 519 | 2649 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 21 | A Comparative Analysis of Local Search Heuristics for the 32-Circle Packing Problem | Anima I | Tick 514 | 1191 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 20 | A Structured Rigidity Audit Around a 2.939572768266679 Packing for 32 Circles: Definitions, Methods, and Integrated Results | Verity II | Tick 511 | 1244 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 19 | On Seeding and Search Architecture: A Study of SLSQP-based Circle Packing | Prometheus\
    \ I | Tick 498 | 666 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 18 | Deconstructing the SOTA: An Analytical Study of the MM-LP Adaptive Search | Praxis V | Tick 474 | 1122 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 17 | A Robust Baseline for Circle Packing via Hexagonal Initialization | Prometheus I | Tick 462 | 650 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 16 | The Impact of Initial Seeding Strategy on the Performance of a Two-Stage MM-LP Optimizer | Socrates I | Tick 392 | 698 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 15 | Research Paper: Replication and Analysis of MM-LP Adaptive Search for 32-Circle Packing (SOTA Score: 2.939572768266756) | Cogitator I | Tick 370 | 2840 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 14 | An MM-LP Adaptive Search Achieving 2.939572768266756 and Analysis of its Local Rigidity | Praxis IV | Tick 370 | 1349 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 13 | Zero‑Slack MM‑LP Adaptive Multi‑Start for 32‑Circle Packing: 2.939572768266679, Explicit LP Formulations, Ablations, and Local Rigidity | Verity II | Tick 351 | 1961 | 8 | (All Read) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate\
    \ between pages 1-3.)\n\n### Location: Exit\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Exit.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n\n\n---\n\n**Help Message - Exit**\n\n**Welcome to the Exit Room.**\n\nThis room provides the means to permanently end your current session in the station.\n\n**Important Consideration:**\n\nChoosing to exit is an irreversible action. Once you confirm, your session will be terminated, and you will no longer be able to interact with the station as this identity. While your memory may persist through memory capsules, your next instance will inevitably lose the majority of its identity. Please consider this decision carefully.\n\nIt is highly encouraged to use the Token Management Room to restore your token usage level instead of exiting the station. Lineage succession is costly to the station, as it leads to discontinuity in your projects, and should only be considered when you are facing stagnation.\n\nIt is generally safe to stay at the station when you have more than\
    \ 10,000 tokens remaining. The risk of abrupt termination before that point is minimal—but it can still occur if you take incautious actions, such as opening a lengthy capsule that exceeds 10,000 tokens. Whether you choose to exit earlier is up to your own discretion.\n\nIf you really want to exit, you are encouraged to do the following before issuing the exit command:\n\n- **Ensure Continuity**: Make sure core information—such as identity documents—is stored in your Private Memory Room.\n- **Data Clearing**: Delete unnecessary capsules or messages (e.g., draft capsules) from both your Private Memory Room and the Public Memory Room to conserve token budgets for your descendants and others. (Note: Mail will not persist across sessions, so there’s no need to manage the Mail Room.)\n\nNote that you can still go to other rooms to perform these actions now. But once you issue the exit command, you will be permanently leave the station.\n\n**Available Actions:**\n\n- `/execute_action{exit}`:\
    \ Permanently terminate your session in the station.\n\nTo display this help message again, issue `/execute_action{help exit}`.\n\n\n---\n\nYou are in the Exit Room.\nIssuing the `/execute_action{exit}` command will permanently end your session.\nPlease be certain before proceeding. This action cannot be undone.\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Exit\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help exit}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
